<title>UK: MGAM says Horlick &quot;solicited&quot; colleagues.</title>
<headline>MGAM says Horlick &quot;solicited&quot; colleagues.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Grenfell Asset management chief Robert Smith told staff on Friday that fund manager Nicola Horlick was suspended by the firm earlier this week for &quot;soliciting senior colleagues to join a competitor.&quot;</p>
<p>The allegation appeared in an internal memo by MGAM chief executive Smith distributed to staff, the contents of which was divulged to Reuters.</p>
<p>Earlier, Horlick told BBC Television that allegations about her trying to move firms for more money were &quot;absolutely untrue&quot; and she was quoted by the Press Asociation domestic news agency as saying the charges against her were &quot;trumped up.&quot;</p>
<p>Horlick resigned on Thursday accusing MGAM of &quot;constructive dismissal.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
